      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After World War II, Yeadon became home to a large middle‑class African‑American community, and its Nile Swim Club was the first African‑American owned club in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
